  "current_trace": [
    "The checked-in combat YAML declares the ten listed values under autoresolve and also declares corresponding movement or AI values. CombatBuildConfig::AutoresolveValues does not declare those ten fields and has no deny_unknown_fields attribute. Its generator instead fills the corresponding EMBEDDED_AUTORESOLVE_PARAMETERS fields from the listed movement/AI values. The build parser validates its selected values; this is not a claim that the entire input is unvalidated.",
    "Pinned serde_derive source emits an ignored-field branch for structs without deny_unknown_fields; the pinned serde-saphyr source accepts Serde IgnoredAny through its deserialize-any path. This is a source-level interpretation of the selected build parser, not an executed macro expansion or YAML parse.",
    "Separately, TacticalCombatConfig contains the full AutoresolveParameters type and validates that retained autoresolve object. Its embedded default parses the same authored YAML; tactical server startup may instead load a supplied YAML, validate it and install a runtime snapshot. The local direct-field search found the retained autoresolve object used in validation and test sources; that search does not establish every possible destructuring, reflection or external consumer.",
    "Strategic resolve_battle reads the build-generated EMBEDDED_AUTORESOLVE_PARAMETERS. In selected consumers, lunge speed constrains melee movement, maximum travel gates attack start, and long-weapon threshold influences retreat. Tactical lunge arrival uses movement.speeds.run, and a bot system selects ai.ordinary.offense. These are distinct source paths with shared-looking values; no actual divergent gameplay run has been observed.",
    "If the same modified YAML is separately consumed by both paths, and only its authored autoresolve lunge-speed value changes while all inputs remain otherwise admissible, the shown tactical parser retains that value while the shown build projection still selects movement.speeds.run. This requires the respective input to be consumed again; it does not imply live reload. The shipped values currently match. This is a conditional source inference; whether a distinct retained tactical autoresolve copy is intentional and whether custom tactical tuning should govern strategic resolution are policy questions, not established product failures."
  ],
